<title>USA: Wall Street stocks higher at start.</title>
<headline>Wall Street stocks higher at start.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow industrials moved higher at the start Friday, bouncing slightly from yesterday's weakness and drawing some strength from the April jobs report.</p>
<p>--Dow Industrials .DJI up seven at 6984.</p>
<p>--Nasdaq Composite .IXIC up five at 1276.</p>
<p>--S&amp;P Index .SPX up one at 800.</p>
<p>--NYSE advance/decline .AD.N 297/197</p>
<p>--Nasdaq advance/decline .AD.O 788/456</p>
<p>--The 30-year long bond off 2/32 to yield 6.92 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1737))</p>
</text>
